hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19282","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us from al-Zuhri, the nephew of Abu Ruhm informed me that he heard Abu Ruhm al-Ghifari, and he was among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who pledged under the tree, say: I raided with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the expedition of Tabuk. When he departed he traveled by night. I went close to him, and drowsiness was cast upon me. I kept waking with my mount near his, frightening me lest I hit his leg in the stirrup, so I held back my mount until my eye overcame me at midnight. My mount mounted his mount, with the leg of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the stirrup, and it hit his leg. I woke only at his saying: Hass. I raised my head and said: Seek forgiveness for me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Ask. He began asking me about those who stayed back of Banu Ghifar, and I informed him. He asked: What did the red tall curly or he said: Short, Abd al-Razzaq doubts, who have livestock at Shaziyyat Sharkh do? I mentioned them among Banu Ghifar but did not recall them until I remembered a group of Aslam. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what prevents one of those, when he stayed back, from carrying an active man in the path of Allah on a camel of his camels. Supplicate that any stay back from the Muhajirun of Quraysh, the Ansar, Aslam, and Ghifar."
"19283","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Salih, Ibn Shihab said: The nephew of Abu Ruhm al-Ghifari informed me that he heard Abu Ruhm, and he was among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who pledged under the tree, say: I raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the expedition of Tabuk. I slept a night at al-Akhdar and went close to him, and he mentioned the meaning of the hadith of Mamar, except that he said: I kept holding back my mount until my eye overcame me part of the night. He said: What did the black short curly who have livestock at Shaziyyat Sharkh do? Thinking they are of Banu Ghifar."
"19284","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, and Ibn Shihab mentioned from Ibn Ukaymah al-Laythi from the nephew of Abu Ruhm al-Ghifari that he heard Abu Ruhm Kulthum ibn Husayn, and he was among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who pledged under the tree, say: I raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the expedition of Tabuk, and he mentioned the hadith, except that he said: I kept holding back my mount from him until my eye overcame me. He said: What did the black curly short do? He said: I said: By Allah, I do not know these among us, until he said: Yes, those who have livestock at Shabakat Sharkh. I remembered them among Banu Ghifar but did not recall them until I remembered that they are a group of Aslam who were allies among us. I said: O Messenger of Allah, those are a group of Aslam who were our allies."
